translation.english:
A cardboard circle with a radius of 5 cm lies on the table. Petya, while possible, attaches cardboard squares with a side of 5 cm to the outside of the circle such that the following conditions are met:
1) each square has one vertex on the boundary of the circle;
2) the squares do not overlap;
3) each subsequent square touches the previous one vertex to vertex.
Determine how many squares Petya can lay out, and prove that the last and first squares will also touch vertex to vertex.

